## Predictions (written before the run)
- countdown is a per-unit tick timer set at spawn: every member of a wave carries the same initial value at first sighting (to within one sample of 200 ticks); it falls by ~1 per tick; the unit is gone within a few thousand ticks of reaching 0
- countdown is per group or set lazily: members differ at first sighting, or the value does not fall linearly, or units leave while it is still far above 0
- the value is species-dependent: different species arriving in the same replicate carry different initial values

